From: Dylan Corrales <deathcamel58@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 11:10:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] drm/panel: jadard-jd9365da-h3: Add the inMusic panels

Add the four JD9365-based 800x1280 MIPI-DSI panels inMusic fits to its
AZ01 devices: urt,umo-9399md-1t, urt,umo-9399md-4t, urt,umoh-9344md-t
and urt,umoh-9522md-1t. The init sequences are the ones the vendor's
bootloader sends, replayed unchanged; the two table-driven ones are
followed by the page 0 select and tearing-effect enable its driver
appends. Timings and DSI flags are the vendor's, except that
9399md-4t runs at 73000 kHz rather than u-boot's 72927, as the vendor
kernel does. At 72927 a Prime 4+ came up with its color channels
rotated.

Supporting them needs three driver changes:

- Per-panel DSI mode flags, as upstream later allowed (eb019688f2a9);
  panels that set none keep the driver's default.
- Set prepare_prev_first, so that the DSI host is up when prepare()
  sends the init sequence (upstream b55a4b5d4769). Without it the
  sequence goes out before the host is up and the panel stays dark.
- With no vdd-supply in the device tree, use the "power" supply as vdd.
  The inMusic device trees predate the vdd/vccio binding.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [adapted backports plus vendor board support]
